e":466},[422,1103,1104],{"class":631},"    User",[422,1106,634],{"class":428},[422,1108,1109],{"class":637},"firstWhere",[422,1111,641],{"class":428},[422,1113,429],{"class":428},[422,1115,1116],{"class":432},"email",[422,1118,429],{"class":428},[422,1120,650],{"class":428},[422,1122,1084],{"class":428},[422,1124,1087],{"class":603},[422,1126,1127],{"class":428},"->",[422,1129,1116],{"class":603},[422,1131,1132],{"class":428},"));\n",[104,1134,1135,1136,1139],{},"Register it in a provider, never in config — a closure in a config file breaks\n",[143,1137,1138],{},"config:cache",". If no author resolves, the tool reports the misconfiguration instead of\nguessing.",[108,1141,1143],{"id":1142},"images","Images",[104,1145,1146,1147,1150,1151,1153,1154,1157,1158,1161,1162,1165,1166,1165,1169,577,1172,1175,1176,1179,1180,1183,1184,1186,1187,1190],{},"MCP's ",[143,1148,1149],{},"tools\u002Fcall"," arguments are plain JSON — there is no binary channel for tool inputs —\nso ",[143,1152,270],{}," accepts either a fetchable ",[143,1155,1156],{},"url"," or base64-encoded ",[143,1159,1160],{},"data"," (exactly one\nof the two). The image type is detected by sniffing the actual bytes, never trusted from a\nfilename or extension; only ",[143,1163,1164],{},"jpeg",", ",[143,1167,1168],{},"png",[143,1170,1171],{},"gif",[143,1173,1174],{},"webp"," are accepted (no ",[143,1177,1178],{},"svg"," — it's a\nstored-XSS vector). Size is capped by ",[143,1181,1182],{},"ink.uploads.max_bytes"," — a HEAD request rejects an\noversized ",[143,1185,1156],{}," by its ",[143,1188,1189],{},"Content-Length"," before the body is downloaded where the server\nadvertises one; the body itself is still measured against the cap either way.",[1192,1193,1194,1197,1198,1200,1201,1204,1205,1208,1209,1212,1213,1216,1217,1219,1220,1222],"caution",{},[683,1195,1196],{},"SSRF stance (accepted risk):"," the ",[143,1199,1156],{}," fetch is scheme-restricted (",[143,1202,1203],{},"http","\u002F",[143,1206,1207],{},"https"," only)\nbut has no host allowlist — it can reach any address your app server can reach, including\ninternal\u002Fprivate ones (e.g. a cloud metadata endpoint). This is an accepted risk, not an\noversight: the caller is already an authenticated, admin-scoped identity trusted to publish\ncontent (",[143,1210,1211],{},"upload-image"," shares ",[143,1214,1215],{},"create-post-tool","'s ",[143,1218,845],{}," Gate ability and ",[143,1221,187],{},"\ntoken ability), not an anonymous or low-privilege one. If your deployment needs a stricter\nboundary — blocking link-local and RFC1918 ranges, for example — enforce it at the network\nlayer in front of the app; there is no host-allowlist config in the package itself.",[412,1224,1226],{"className":414,"code":1225,"filename":416,"language":417,"meta":418,"style":418},"'uploads' => [\n    'disk' => 'public',       \u002F\u002F matches the Filament featured-image field's disk\n    'directory' => 'ink',     \u002F\u002F matches its directory too — panel and MCP uploads share a home\n    'max_bytes' => 3 * 1024 * 1024,\n],\n",[143,1227,1228,1241,1264,1287,1313],{"__ignoreMap":418},[422,1229,1230,1232,1235,1237,1239],{"class":424,"line":425},[422,1231,429],{"class":428},[422,1233,1234],{"class":432},"uploads",[422,1236,429],{"class":428},[422,1238,438],{"class":428},[422,1240,441],{"class":428},[422,1242,1243,1245,1248,1250,1252,1254,1257,1259,1261],{"class":424,"line":444},[422,1244,447],{"class":428},[422,1246,1247],{"class":432},"disk",[422,1249,429],{"class":428},[422,1251,438],{"class":428},[422,1253,498],{"class":428},[422,1255,1256],{"class":432},"public",[422,1258,429],{"class":428},[422,1260,650],{"class":428},[422,1262,1263],{"class":524},"       \u002F\u002F matches the Filament featured-image field's disk\n",[422,1265,1266,1268,1271,1273,1275,1277,1280,1282,1284],{"class":424,"line":460},[422,1267,447],{"class":428},[422,1269,1270],{"class":432},"directory",[422,1272,429],{"class":428},[422,1274,438],{"class":428},[422,1276,498],{"class":428},[422,1278,1279],{"class":432},"ink",[422,1281,429],{"class":428},[422,1283,650],{"class":428},[422,1285,1286],{"class":524},"     \u002F\u002F matches its directory too — panel and MCP uploads share a home\n",[422,1288,1289,1291,1294,1296,1298,1301,1304,1307,1309,1311],{"class":424,"line":466},[422,1290,447],{"class":428},[422,1292,1293],{"class":432},"max_bytes",[422,1295,429],{"class":428},[422,1297,438],{"class":428},[422,1299,1300],{"class":599}," 3",[422,1302,1303],{"class":428}," *",[422,1305,1306],{"class":599}," 1024",[422,1308,1303],{"class":428},[422,1310,1306],{"class":599},[422,1312,506],{"class":428},[422,1314,1315],{"class":424,"line":473},[422,1316,463],{"class":428},[1192,1318,1319,1328,1329,1331,1332,1334,1335,1339,1340,1342,1343,1345,1346,1349,1350,1352],{},[683,1320,1321,1323,1324,1327],{},[143,1322,1293],{}," and PHP's ",[143,1325,1326],{},"post_max_size"," (base64 uploads only):"," the base64 ",[143,1330,1160],{}," path is\nbound by PHP's ",[143,1333,1326],{}," — and any webserver\u002Fproxy body-size limit — ",[1336,1337,1338],"em",{},"before Laravel\never boots",". base64 inflates the binary size by ~4\u002F3, so an oversized payload is rejected by\nPHP itself: the client gets a raw PHP warning wrapped in an HTTP 200, not a clean JSON-RPC\nerror, and no app-level check (this one included) can catch it. The 3MB default (≈4MB\nbase64-encoded) stays safely under a common 5-8M ",[143,1341,1326],{}," floor; raise both together\nif you need a higher cap, keeping ",[143,1344,1326],{}," comfortably above ",[143,1347,1348],{},"max_bytes * 4\u002F3",". The\n",[143,1351,1156],{}," path has no such ceiling — the image is fetched by this server's own HTTP client, not\ncarried in the MCP request body at all — so prefer it for anything larger than a few MB.",[104,1354,1355,1356,1358,1359,1361,1362,1364,1365,1368,1369,1371,1372,1375],{},"The tool returns a ",[143,1357,491],{}," (pass it as ",[143,1360,193],{}," to ",[143,1363,1215],{}," \u002F\n",[143,1366,1367],{},"update-post-tool","), a public ",[143,1370,1156],{},", and a ready-to-paste ",[143,1373,1374],{},"markdown"," snippet for in-content\nimages:",[412,1377,1381],{"className":1378,"code":1379,"language":1380,"meta":418,"style":418},"language-json shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","{\n  \"path\": \"ink\u002F01hz...webp\",\n  \"url\": \"https:\u002F\u002Fexample.test\u002Fstorage\u002Fink\u002F01hz...webp\",\n  \"markdown\": \"![A dashboard screenshot](https:\u002F\u002Fexample.test\u002Fstorage\u002Fink\u002F01hz...webp)\"\n}\n","json",[143,1382,1383,1388,1410,1429,1447],{"__ignoreMap":418},[422,1384,1385],{"class":424,"line":425},[422,1386,1387],{"class":428},"{\n",[422,1389,1390,1393,1395,1398,1400,1403,1406,1408],{"class":424,"line":444},[422,1391,1392],{"class":428},"  \"",[422,1394,491],{"class":1074},[422,1396,1397],{"class":428},"\"",[422,1399,693],{"class":428},[422,1401,1402],{"class":428}," \"",[422,1404,1405],{"class":432},"ink\u002F01hz...webp",[422,1407,1397],{"class":428},[422,1409,506],{"class":428},[422,1411,1412,1414,1416,1418,1420,1422,1425,1427],{"class":424,"line":460},[422,1413,1392],{"class":428},[422,1415,1156],{"class":1074},[422,1417,1397],{"class":428},[422,1419,693],{"class":428},[422,1421,1402],{"class":428},[422,1423,1424],{"class":432},"https:\u002F\u002Fexample.test\u002Fstorage\u002Fink\u002F01hz...webp",[422,1426,1397],{"class":428},[422,1428,506],{"class":428},[422,1430,1431,1433,1435,1437,1439,1441,1444],{"class":424,"line":466},[422,1432,1392],{"class":428},[422,1434,1374],{"class":1074},[422,1436,1397],{"class":428},[422,1438,693],{"class":428},[422,1440,1402],{"class":428},[422,1442,1443],{"class":432},"![A dashboard screenshot](https:\u002F\u002Fexample.test\u002Fstorage\u002Fink\u002F01hz...webp)",[422,1445,1446],{"class":428},"\"\n",[422,1448,1449],{"class":424,"line":473},[422,1450,1451],{"class":428},"}\n",[104,1453,1454,1456,1457,1459,1460,1462,1463,1465,1466,1469,1470,1472,1473,1476,1477,1480,1481,577,1484,1487,1488,577,1491,1494,1495,1498],{},[143,1455,193],{}," on ",[143,1458,1215],{}," \u002F ",[143,1461,1367],{}," only accepts a path\n",[143,1464,1211],{}," itself produced — it's validated against the uploads disk and directory, so\nan agent can't point it at an arbitrary file. Pass ",[143,1467,1468],{},"featured_image: null"," on\n",[143,1471,1367],{}," to clear it. Rendering assumes the public disk with ",[143,1474,1475],{},"storage:link"," run —\nthe six ",[143,1478,1479],{},"asset('storage\u002F…')"," call sites documented in the README are unchanged by this\nfeature. Rendered post images get ",[143,1482,1483],{},"loading=\"lazy\"",[143,1485,1486],{},"decoding=\"async\""," automatically on\nboth render paths (",[143,1489,1490],{},"Post::toHtml()",[143,1492,1493],{},"Post::toSafeHtml()","), leaving any attribute the\nauthor declared by hand alone; there is no automatic resizing or ",[143,1496,1497],{},"srcset"," generation yet, so an\noversized source image still costs bandwidth and LCP — keep uploads reasonably sized until a\nresizing pipeline ships.",[108,1500,1502],{"id":1501},"scheduling","Scheduling",[104,1504,1505,1506,1509,1510,1513,1514,1517,1518,1520,1521,1524],{},"A post with ",[143,1507,1508],{},"status: \"published\""," and a future ",[143,1511,1512],{},"published_at"," is scheduled, not published\nimmediately: ",[143,1515,1516],{},"Post::published()"," is evaluated at query time, so the post appears on the\npublic index\u002Fshow\u002Ffeed\u002Fsitemap the moment the clock passes ",[143,1519,1512],{},", with no queue or\ncommand involved. Its signed preview URL (",[143,1522,1523],{},"generate-preview-url-tool",") keeps working right\nup until then.",[108,1526,1528],{"id":1527},"content-format","Content format",[104,1530,1531,1532,1534],{},"The tools store the ",[683,1533,1374],{}," you send, exactly as the Filament editor does; they do not\nconvert it to HTML. Rendering — and therefore HTML sanitisation — happens at read time\nthrough your application's markdown configuration.",[1192,1536,1537,1538,1541],{},"Posts created by ink 2.1 and earlier hold rendered HTML. The\n",[143,1539,1540],{},"convert_html_post_content_to_markdown"," migration converts them and prints the ids of any\nrow it could not convert cleanly, so you can review those by hand.",[108,1543,1545],{"id":1544},"extending","Extending",[104,1547,1548,1549,1552,1553,1556,1557,1560,1561,1564,1565,1165,1568,506,1571,577,1574,1577,1578,1581],{},"Custom blog tools should extend ",[143,1550,1551],{},"Relaticle\\Ink\\Mcp\\BlogTool"," rather than\n",[143,1554,1555],{},"Laravel\\Mcp\\Server\\Tool",". Its ",[143,1558,1559],{},"handle()"," is ",[143,1562,1563],{},"final"," and performs authorization before\ndelegating, so a new tool cannot ship without it. Declare ",[143,1566,1567],{},"ability()",[143,1569,1570],{},"tokenAbility()",[143,1572,1573],{},"model()",[143,1575,1576],{},"run()","; override ",[143,1579,1580],{},"resolveRecord()"," when the tool operates on one record.",[1583,1584,1585],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .sHwdD, html code.shiki .sHwdD{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-default:#546E7A;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#676E95;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .def